{
  "opening": "This release introduces the new TLRU cache algorithm and enhances the key generation utilities for methods. It also adds introspection capabilities to decorators and deprecates older, less efficient caching strategies.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The TLRUCache class must be available as a new cache implementation that combines time-to-live and least-recently-used eviction policies. Existing TTLCache and LRU-based caches should continue to function with their standard get, set, and pop behaviors."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "refactor_note": "Internal refactoring of time-aware caches is not visible in the public API; ensure existing TTLCache and RRCache instances maintain consistent behavior for clear, get, pop, and setdefault operations."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "Decorators such as @cached and @cachedmethod must expose their configuration parameters (e.g., maxsize, ttl) as attributes on the returned wrapper function. These attributes should reflect the values passed during decorator initialization."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17",
      "text": "The methodkey function must be exported from the keys module to generate cache keys based on the method name and arguments. It should work seamlessly with @cachedmethod to distinguish calls across different methods or instances."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "Decorators like @cached and @cachedmethod must provide a cache_clear attribute or method that clears all entries from the associated cache instance. Calling this should reset the cache size to zero without removing the decorated function."
    },
    {
      "id": "m27",
      "text": "The @cached decorator must expose a cache_info attribute that returns an object containing statistics such as hits, misses, and current cache size. This info object should match the structure expected by users familiaring themselves with functools.lru_cache stats."
    },
    {
      "id": "m65",
      "text": "The typedmethodkey decorator must be available in the keys module to create cache keys that include the argument types. It should behave similarly to typedkey but be specifically designed for use with method caching scenarios."
    },
    {
      "id": "m69",
      "text": "The MRUCache class must emit a deprecation warning when instantiated or used. Users should be directed to use alternative cache implementations like LRUCache or TLRUCache instead."
    },
    {
      "id": "m71",
      "text": "The expire method on TTLCache must return an iterable of expired (key, value) pairs rather than modifying the cache in place or returning None. This allows consumers to process expired items before they are removed."
    },
    {
      "id": "m72",
      "text": "The expire method on TLRUCache must return an iterable of expired (key, value) pairs, ensuring consistency with the TTLCache interface. Expired items should be identified based on both age and recency according to the TLRU policy."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that all new public names are correctly exported and that deprecation warnings trigger appropriately. Ensure backward compatibility for existing cache algorithms while introducing the new TLRU variant."
}
